  "actual_GitHub_PR": {
    "body": "The verified theorem is published as **An even-strand Markov calculus for classical and virtual links**, Alec Kriebel: [DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23131001](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23131001). The record contains the five-page research note and reproducible verification package.\n\nThe theorem supplies four classical and eight virtual reversible algebraic scheme families classifying ordinary oriented unframed link closures through tagged even-strand braid states. Arbitrary finite word blocks and explicit syntactic support bounds are part of the formulation. The universal soundness/completeness proof imports the established unrestricted Alexander and Markov theorems; finite computations supplement it. No minimality, uniformly bounded geometric locality, certificate-search algorithm, plat, framed, transverse or welded result is claimed.\n\n**Historical priority remains unresolved.** Nencka's authenticated 1996 announcement is credited. We could not access the identified fuller 1998 article, 1999 chapter, or catalogued 1996 preprint CPT96/P.3381 to complete their priority assessment. Publication follows the human user's explicit authorization to publish this qualified research note. It does not certify historical novelty, a first resolution, or present openness, and unavailable text is not evidence that earlier work is absent or invalid.\n\nTwo fresh independent whole-package adversarial reviews found no substantive issues. Each reconstructed the universal proof, reproduced the 7,114 diagnostics, rebuilt the exact verification archive, and checked the source and all five PDF pages; separate necessary-invariant attacks also passed. These are AI reviews, and the research note has not undergone conventional human peer review or formal proof certification. AI tools were used extensively in construction, drafting and verification.\n\nThe operative publication package is `draft_pr_publication_program_20260930/audits/pr50_10600042/publication_package_v3`. Current review, exact public-download verification and spreadsheet readback records are in `qualified_publication_20261004` and the two `qualified_round*_adversary_20261004` folders. The tracker row is `'Math Puzzles'!A18:D18`, independently checked for exact contents and uniqueness.\n\nThe fifteen original scientific files from submitted head `7260315f8b8b193020c09d4ef6df9d943a3a13ff` are retained unchanged as dated historical inputs. Their earlier candidate/review wording is superseded for present acceptance by the qualified publication, `acceptance.json` and `CURRENT_RESULT.md`. Original substantive attempts remain **1/5**; this validation and publication added no central proof attempts.\n",
    "headRefOid": "7260315f8b8b193020c09d4ef6df9d943a3a13ff",
